.TH SYSMOND 8 "2024" "sysmon 3.1.0" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
sysmond \- small system monitoring daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysmond
.RB [ \-ftpVh ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-i
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR level ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sysmond
samples cpu, memory, swap, load and disk usage at a fixed interval,
plus whatever its plugins provide, and keeps the values and a short
history in memory.
Clients query it over a unix socket, usually with
.BR sysmonctl (1).
It can also expose its metrics to Prometheus over HTTP and evaluate
simple threshold alerts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " file"
Read the configuration from
.IR file .
.TP
.B \-f
Stay in the foreground instead of daemonizing.
.TP
.B \-t
Check the configuration and alert rules, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-i " seconds"
Sampling interval, overrides the configuration.
.TP
.BI \-l " level"
Log level: error, warn, info or debug.
.TP
.B \-p
Print every sample to standard output (with
.BR \-f ).
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Re-read the configuration file and reopen the log file.
The socket, HTTP listener and plugins are not affected.
.TP
.BR SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Exit cleanly, removing the socket and the pid file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sysmond.conf
Configuration, see
.I contrib/sysmond.conf
for every key.
.TP
.I /tmp/sysmond.sock
Default control socket.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/sysmon/plugins/
Default plugin directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sysmond -f -c /etc/sysmond.conf
sysmonctl get cpu_usage_percent
curl -s localhost:9273/metrics
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sysmonctl (1),
.BR proc (5),
.BR statvfs (3)
